summary:
Design for slice 2's safety, classification and checks (core gate plus Lean facts). Five parts.

(1) A facts extension, DeclFacts.typeConsts, added to the existing value probe. With it, every closure (statement closure, held set, "mentions") comes from what Lean elaborated, never from .ilean refs. Without it, a definition reached only through a class or structure field type, an instance's class, or an inductive's constructor types escapes RV-7 and backstop (b).

(2) A new pure core module, packages/core/src/review/ (named so it does not clash with core/src/edit/session.ts). It holds:
- elaborated closures (R_stmt, 'meaning' versus 'uses' constants);
- one total, deterministic ownership map from every B→S difference to a review item, plus content keys and a telelean ledger of everything telelean itself writes;
- RV-7 classification by effect in Lean, recomputed on every judged state;
- the RV-5 item-dependency graph (all five bullets), with SCC handling, Accept blockers, group-Accept selection and decline/leave-accepted cascades;
- B.1 per-inference permitted sets with E(T). A source contributes a footprint only through the user's own unchanged proof from B, or through a session Result that passes its own inference in the same state ("counts like one of your own"; it creates the Result→Result dependency). So no Claude proof widens the set it is judged against.
- judgeState: per-inference footprint, B.2 and not-proved checks, plus global rules (ES-2 step preset with text, meaning and constant-set comparison; new-axiom against B; B.3 arrows via the ledger and a proposed propose_arrow tool; B.4 kinds; G5/CF-3; cycles; DO-1/DO-3 exact repeats);
- RV-6 hidden-result computation through a masked facts overlay given to buildProject. A footprint decomposition makes this Lean-free. It also fixes a 1d leak: a downstream card's "result hidden" chip appears only when the target was proved.
- applyBackstop (Appendix B, never reused). It re-derives ownership from B→F, verifies accepted content keys and own-Accepts, and checks arrows, B.2–B.4 and SCC closure.

(3) Runner wiring: CheckContext.session, stored step-start facts, a final check at Apply with a selective G4 rerun, and removal of the unreachable D-21 rebase.

(4) Eight buildable sub-slices, in dependency order.

(5) A test plan with core states built on fake facts and FakeBackend session scripts for S1, S4, S5, S6, S14, S15, S17, S18 and S22, plus an RV-6 non-interference property test. 19 open questions, each with a recommended answer.

