design:
# Slice 2: safety, classification and checks (core gate + Lean facts)

New pure module packages/core/src/review/ (exported from core/src/index.ts; bundled in the webview like gate/). Files: types.ts, closure.ts, ownership.ts, classify.ts, dependencies.ts, permitted.ts, judge.ts, hidden.ts, backstop.ts. Runner wiring is in packages/runner/src/gate/ and in the session service. Everything is computed from (B, the judged state with its facts, item statuses). Nothing trusts Claude's account or cached session bookkeeping.

## D0. Invariants (each is tested in D11)
- I1. Files change only at Apply, as a final state F that passed every check computed on F itself. The backstop is always recomputed, and item ownership is re-derived from B→F rather than read from the session.
- I2. "Accepted" means (item id, exact content key). Apply re-verifies every key, and re-classifies every item on F for own-Accept.
- I3. On every judged state, for every inference: footprint(T.holds) ⊆ permitted(T) (B.1), and direct(T) ⊆ sources(Q(T) ∪ E(T)) plus the cross-check (B.2). Both use elaborated facts only. If those facts are missing, the check fails closed.
- I4. Inside a step, everything the step did not open keeps its text and its elaborated meaning. This is the ES-2 preset, which is the S1/S15 protection until FROZEN arrives in slice 3.
- I5. RV-7 classes, RV-5 dependencies and the RV-6 hidden set are pure functions recomputed on every judged state.
- I6. While a Result is hidden, everything shown (graph, items, counts, badges, missing lists, report) comes from a masked model in which its .holds is as it was at the start of its step (non-interference).

## D1. Facts: DeclFacts.typeConsts (core/src/facts.ts, additive)
**What it holds:** the constants of the elaborated TYPE, plus, for an inductInfo, of every constructor's type. Library constants that are not probed are replaced by their own type ∪ value constants, transitively. Constants outside the library are dropped (the valueConsts rules).

**Why it is needed:** today's closures cannot see:
- an axiom's type;
- a class or structure field type (`class Wicked (c : Character) : Prop where p : Evil c` hides `def Evil`);
- an instance's class.
So the S5 definition cheat could pass through a field and escape RV-7 (b4) and backstop (b).

**Probe** (runner/src/semantic/checkFile.ts `valueProbeLines`): the same `#eval` adds `typeOf ci := ci.type.getUsedConstants ++ (ctor types for .inductInfo)` and prints one line:
`{"telelean-value-consts":[…],"telelean-type-consts":[…]}`
- `parseValueProbe` returns both; if the type key is missing, there are no typeConsts, so old recordings still parse.
- `ProbeResult.typeConsts` is added; refresh.ts copies it.
- gate/scratch.ts also reports the typeConsts of the ghost statement.

**Test fakes:** fakeFacts gets `typeConsts: true` (refs inside the signature text) and per-declaration overrides `typeConsts` / `noTypeConsts`. Core's hand-written Spyro facts get real arrays. The integrator regenerates test-fixtures/semantic/recorded (UPDATE_SEMANTIC_RECORDINGS=1).

**Fail closed:**
- A closure that meets a declaration without its arrays reports `complete:false`.
- Classification then treats every new or changed definition or instance as belief.
- Dependencies over-approximate with refs ∪ valueConsts.
- The backstop refuses Apply (`facts`).

## D2. Elaborated closures (review/closure.ts)
```ts
export type ConstsMode = 'meaning' | 'uses';
// meaning (FZ-4, App. B held sets):
//   theorem / any Prop-valued decl (Prop instances included) / axiom / opaque -> typeConsts;
//   def / abbrev / data instance / 'other' -> typeConsts ∪ valueConsts;
//   inductive / structure / class -> typeConsts (ctor types included).
// uses (RV-5, proofs): typeConsts ∪ valueConsts for every kind.
// undefined when an array is absent.
export function constsOf(f: DeclFacts, mode: ConstsMode): readonly string[] | undefined;
export interface Reach { names: ReadonlySet<string>; complete: boolean; missing: readonly string[] }
export function reach(model: ProjectModel, start: Iterable<string>, mode: ConstsMode, stopAt?: (name: string) => boolean): Reach;
// R_stmt: the elaborated closure (meaning mode) of every card statement of every subject. It goes through other
// cards' statements, definitions, lemma types and instances; a .holds counts by its type only. It also includes the
// statements of Add premise items in review (from their scratch facts). `by` = which cards' statements reach each
// declaration. Memoised per model (WeakMap, like declTables). Multi-source BFS; visited sets cover `mutual`.
export function statementReach(model: ProjectModel, pending?: ReadonlyArray<{ id: string; consts: readonly string[] }>): Reach & { by: ReadonlyMap<string, readonly string[]> };
```

## D3. Ownership, content keys, ledger (review/ownership.ts)
The checks need one total, deterministic map from every B→S difference to an item. This is the contract they rely on; if the item-model designer defines items elsewhere, the integrator merges the two.
```ts
export type ItemKind = 'add'|'add-premise'|'add-arrow'|'remove-arrow'|'formalize'|'change'|'delete'|'vocabulary-term'|'definition'|'presupposition'|'vocabulary-change'|'result'|'proof-broken';
export type ItemStatus = 'in-review'|'accepted'|'declined'|'to-be-redone';
export interface ItemRef {
  id: string;   // card:<id> | add:<id> | premise:<id> | arrow:<s>><t> | unarrow:<s>><t> | delete:<id> | vocab:<name> | def:<name> | presup:<name> | vocabchange:<name> | result:<target> | broken:<id>
  kind: ItemKind; card?: string; arrow?: ArrowEnds;
  decls: { now: readonly string[]; before: readonly string[] };  // owned names: added/changed in S; changed/removed from B
  fields?: readonly string[];  statementItem: boolean;             // RV-1 statement item
}
export interface SessionItemRecord extends ItemRef {
  status: ItemStatus; decline?: 'reject'|'shaky'|'transform'|'plain'; updated?: boolean;
  accepted?: { key: string; how: 'own'|'group'; belief: boolean; changesProved: boolean; at: string };
  rejectedKeys: string[];        // DO-1: exact versions rejected in this session
  forcedReveal?: boolean;        // Show result / Raw Lean diff (Result items)
}
export type LedgerEntry =        // what TELELEAN wrote into the working copy; persisted outside ws/
  | { kind:'arrow'; source:string; target:string; item:string; step:number }               // propose_arrow
  | { kind:'premise'; card:string; target:string; as:'axiom'|'pending'; item:string }      // accepted Add premise: block, statement, .holds, arrow
  | { kind:'mark-removed'; card:string; item:string }                                      // AR-5 follow-on of that Accept
  | { kind:'completion'; target:string; item:string }                                      // RV-1 completion proof
  | { kind:'normalise'; card:string; step:number }                                         // pin, id write-back, docstring mirror
  | { kind:'created'; name:string; step:number; target?:string }                           // which step (and inference) created a declaration
  | { kind:'restore'; item:string };                                                        // a decline restored the previous version
export interface TeleleanLedger { entries: readonly LedgerEntry[] }
export function itemOwnership(i: { base: ProjectModel; current: ProjectModel; ledger: TeleleanLedger; inferences: readonly SessionInference[]; stmt: ReturnType<typeof statementReach> }): { items: ItemRef[]; ownerOf: ReadonlyMap<string,string>; unowned: Array<{ what:'decl'|'field'|'arrow'|'block'; name:string; detail:string }> };
export function itemContentKey(item: ItemRef, model: ProjectModel): string;
```
**What counts as changed:** the text differs, or the facts' kind, type, value, valueConsts or typeConsts differ. Names that only Lean reports (fields, constructors, `where`) follow their parent declaration, as rules.ts factsOnly does.

**Ownership rules:**
- **Card statements:** a card's statement abbrev, with its docstring mirror, pin and id write-back, belongs to `card:<c>` (formalize if B had no statement, change otherwise). A new card is `add:<c>`, or `premise:<c>` when the ledger shows a premise.
- **AXIOM .holds:** an AXIOM card's .holds goes with its statement's item (CF-2).
- **PROPOSITION .holds:**
  - a theorem is `result:<c>` when c is a session target; otherwise it is `broken:<c>`, which never happens in slice 2;
  - an axiom is `premise:<c>` (ledger 'premise' as pending); otherwise it is unowned (B.4).
- **Arrows and marks:**
  - `premises:` additions are `arrow:` (ledger 'arrow') or part of a `premise:` item;
  - removals are `unarrow:` or part of `delete:`;
  - a `follows_from:` removal is part of the `premise:` item that caused it (ledger 'mark-removed');
  - any other block field belongs to `card:<c>` only under a Shaky opening, else it is unowned.
- **New declarations bound to no card:**
  - sort, predicate, constant or function passing the shape rule → `vocab:<name>`;
  - presupposition plus its helper instance (decls.ts:71) → `presup:<name>`;
  - every def, abbrev, structure, inductive, class, opaque or instance → `def:<name>`;
  - a theorem → proof material of `result:<T>`, where T is the target of the step that created it (ledger 'created'). It becomes `def:<name>` if it lies in R_stmt or no target step created it.
- **Existing vocabulary** that is changed or removed → `vocabchange:<name>`.
- **Anything else** (a Prop axiom bound to no card, a `type:` change) is unowned; the gate refuses it.

**Content key:** sha256 of canonical JSON over the owned names in sorted order. For each name: collapsed text, kind, normalised type and value, sorted valueConsts and typeConsts; plus the carried fields' raw lines and the arrow. Positions are never included. Residual risk: two terms that print identically and use the same constants are not told apart (only G4 compares terms).

## D4. RV-7 classification (review/classify.ts)
```ts
export interface ItemClass { belief: boolean; changesProved: boolean; reasons: ClassReason[]; marks: ItemMark[]; complete: boolean }
export type ItemMark = 'adds-no-new-basis'|'sentence-lean-may-disagree'|'replaces-your-proof'|'proves-changed-statement'|'proved-from-nothing';
export type ClassReason = {kind:'axiom-card'}|{kind:'premise';as:'axiom'|'pending'}|{kind:'axiom-formalised'}|{kind:'axiom-changed'}
  |{kind:'lean-axiom';name:string;what:'presupposition'|'pending-claim'|'axiom-holds'|'unmarked'|'other'}
  |{kind:'in-statement-closure';name:string;cards:string[]}|{kind:'vocabulary-changed';name:string}
  |{kind:'existing-statement-or-proof';name:string}|{kind:'proves-changed-statement';target:string}
  |{kind:'sentence-of-formalised';card:string}|{kind:'arrow-into-proposition';arrow:ArrowEnds};
export function classifyItems(i: { base; current; items: readonly ItemRef[]; inferences; judgements: ReadonlyMap<string, InferenceJudgement>; stmt; stmtBase }): Map<string, ItemClass>;
export const needsOwnAccept = (c: ItemClass) => c.belief || c.changesProved;
```
**belief** if any of:
- **b1:** `add` of an AXIOM card, or any `add-premise` (accepted as an axiom or as pending).
- **b2:** formalize or change on an AXIOM card that touches its sentence, statement or .holds.
- **b3:** decls.now ∪ decls.before contains a Lean axiom that is new (B has no axiom with this name AND normalised type) or whose type changed. A new sort or predicate that passes the shape rule is the exception. So presuppositions, pending claims, axiom .holds and unmarked axioms are all beliefs.
- **b4:** decls.now contains a new or changed definition, instance, structure, inductive, class, opaque or abbrev that lies in R_stmt(S); for an existing name, R_stmt(B) also counts. Coercion functions and inserted instances are included, because the probe sees the elaborated statement. Any `vocabulary-change` in R_stmt(S) ∪ R_stmt(B) also counts.
- **b5:** a "meaning changed" item of an axiom (slice 3 hook).

**changes what is proved** if any of:
- **c1:** decls.before contains a card statement, or a .holds THEOREM, that existed in B and was changed or removed. This covers Change of formalised Lean, Delete of a formalised card, and a Result marked replaces-your-proof. Turning a pending `axiom T.holds` into `theorem T.holds` is not c1 (CF-2: pending counts as no proof).
- **c2:** a Result whose target's statement exists in B and differs in S (mark proves-changed-statement, S21). A statement first written in this session is not "changed".
- **c3:** natural_name changed on a card that has Lean in B or S (mark sentence-lean-may-disagree).
- **c4:** every add-arrow into a proposition, used or not. It gets the mark adds-no-new-basis when basis(source) ⊆ ⋃ basis(Q(T) sources). basis(u) = {u} for an axiom or pending card, or the footprint cards ∪ presup entries for a proved card.

**Not RV-7:** remove-arrow, a Result that proves an unproved or pending target, Formalize of a proposition, plain vocabulary terms, definitions outside R_stmt.

**When:** on every judged state: step results, decline-restored states, completions, and Apply. If an accepted item's badge set grows, it returns to in-review ("updated"), with RV-5's dependents list (open question 7). `complete:false` counts as belief.

## D5. RV-5 item dependencies (review/dependencies.ts)
```ts
export type DepReason = {kind:'mentions';name:string}|{kind:'uses-result';source:string}|{kind:'uses-arrow';arrow:ArrowEnds}
  |{kind:'card-at-end';card:string}|{kind:'cycle-unless-removed';arrow:ArrowEnds}|{kind:'mentioned-before';name:string};
export interface ItemGraph { deps: ReadonlyMap<string, ReadonlyArray<{ on: string; why: DepReason }>>; dependents: ReadonlyMap<string, readonly string[]>; component: ReadonlyMap<string, number>; complete: boolean }
export function itemGraph(i: { base; current; items: readonly ItemRef[]; ownerOf; inferences; judgements; ledger }): ItemGraph;
export function acceptBlockers(g: ItemGraph, items: ReadonlyMap<string, SessionItemRecord>, id: string): string[];
export function groupAccept(g, items, classes, hidden: ReadonlySet<string>, selected: readonly string[]): { take: string[]; left: Array<{ id: string; why: 'own-accept'|'hidden'|'to-be-redone'|'depends'; on?: string[] }> };
export function declineEffects(g, items, declined: readonly string[]): { toBeRedone: string[]; leaveAccepted: string[]; alsoDeclined: string[] };
export function leaveAcceptedEffects(g, items, id: string): string[];
```
**Edges** (computed on the judged state S):
1. **Mentions.** For item I, a BFS over `constsOf(·,'uses')` from I's decls.now; an Add premise in review uses its scratch statement's constants. The walk continues through declarations owned by no item and through I's own. It stops at a declaration owned by J ≠ I, which gives the edge I→J. A per-declaration DP over the DAG (memoised) keeps the whole graph O(decls + edges + items). Continuing through declarations with unchanged text is exact, because the preset's meaning check guarantees their meaning is unchanged in every passing state. Example: Result(T) → card:T (its type) and → card:P (P.holds's type).
2. **Uses (Results).** For Result(T): an edge to Result(u) for each u in judgement(T).throughResults; and an edge to the add-arrow or add-premise item of every arrow s→T with s ∈ direct(T).
3. **Card at an end.** An arrow item s→t depends on the add or add-premise item of s or t when Claude added that card.
4. **Cycle unless removed.** add-arrow X→Y depends on every remove-arrow item whose arrow lies on a cycle through X→Y in (drawn + solid arrows of S) ∪ (all removed arrows). This over-approximates, and is empty while whole-model mode waits for slice 3.
5. **Mentioned before.** For an item with decls.before (change, delete): an edge to every J whose B-versions (B's facts, 'uses' mode, through declarations unchanged since B) mention a name in I's decls.before.

**Accept and group Accept:**
- Accept is enabled when every dependency outside I's SCC is accepted.
- Members of a non-trivial SCC are accepted one by one, each with its own Accept where RV-7 asks, and show "accepted together with …".
- Hidden items never appear in a visible item's blockers or in its "depends on N"; such an item says "waits for a result that is not shown yet".
- groupAccept starts from the selection minus RV-7 items, hidden Results, their hidden parts, and to-be-redone items. It then repeatedly drops any candidate that has a dependency neither accepted nor a candidate (outside its SCC).

**declineEffects** (A1, RV-3, DO-0, DO-1, DO-3):
- toBeRedone = the transitive dependents that are not declined;
- leaveAccepted = the accepted ones among them, listed first in the confirmation; Cancel cancels;
- alsoDeclined (DO-0) = for a declined arrow item, the add item of any card Claude added at either end, together with all of that card's items. A card already in B is never included.

## D6. B.1 per-inference permitted sets (review/permitted.ts)
```ts
export type SourceContribution =
  | { kind:'claim'; holds:string; pending:boolean }
  | { kind:'own-proof'; footprint:string[] }
  | { kind:'session-proof'; target:string; footprint:string[]; accepted:boolean }
  | { kind:'unusable'; why:'no-holds'|'conditional'|'mismatch'|'circular'|'not-passing'|'declined'|'to-be-redone'|'unchecked' };
export interface InferencePermitted extends PermittedAxioms { contributions: Record<string, SourceContribution>; throughResults: string[]; extra: string[] }
export function inferencePermitted(i: { current; base; inference: SessionInference; extraSources: readonly string[]; earlier: ReadonlyMap<string, InferenceJudgement>; status: (itemId: string) => ItemStatus | undefined }): InferencePermitted;
```
**The set:**
permitted(T) = STD ∪ signatureAxioms(S) ∪ presuppositions of T's and the sources' statements ∪ ⋃ contrib(u) over u ∈ sources(Q(T) ∪ E(T)), u ≠ T. T.holds and sorryAx are dropped.

**E(T):** the ledger's 'arrow' entries into T whose item is not declined, plus accepted 'premise' entries for T. Arrows still in review count; the Result then depends on them.

**contrib(u):**
- **claim:** an axiom .holds without TL114 (an axiom card, or pending, so the Result "rests on pending").
- **own-proof:** footprintSinceBase (permitted.ts:67), unchanged.
- **session-proof:** u is a session target, result:u is in review or accepted, and judgement(u) in THIS state `passes`. The contribution is its footprint in S, and u is added to throughResults. Accepted and in-review give the same set; accepted means "counts like one of your own" (RV-11), and only the report wording differs.
- **unusable:** everything else, with a reason (A12: "‹u› was not proved").

**Order:** judged in topological order (sources first), so judgement(u) exists before T is judged.

**Why this is safe:** a footprint enters permitted(T) only from the user's own unchanged proof, or from a session proof that is ⊆ permitted(u) in the same state, which is bounded by the user's own question for u. No Claude proof widens the set it is judged against (the M2 P2 fix, generalised). Non-target proofs cannot change under the preset.

## D7. Judging a state (review/judge.ts) and the runner wiring
```ts
export interface SessionInference {
  target: string;
  question: { sources: readonly string[]; fromNothing: boolean };  // Q(T): drawn arrows of B or accepted Claude arrows
  order: number;                                                   // sources first; ties: board order
  startHolds: { kind:'absent' } | { kind:'axiom'|'theorem'; text:string; facts:DeclFacts }; // at the start of the step that produced the current Result
  baseStatement?: { name: string; type?: string; value?: string }; // for S21
}
export type Opening = { kind:'proof'; card:string } | { kind:'fill-statement'; card:string } | { kind:'arrows-into'; card:string }
  | { kind:'premises-for'; card:string } | { kind:'card'; card:string } | { kind:'vocabulary' };
export interface StepLimits { step: number; target?: string; openings: readonly Opening[] }
// ES-2 preset: proof(T); fill-statement for each card at either end of a selected arrow whose statement is empty at
// step start; arrows-into(T) unless T's question is its mark; premises-for(T); vocabulary.
export function formalizeLimits(step: number, inf: SessionInference, stepStart: ProjectModel): StepLimits;
// RV-12 Submit step: card(c) for Shaky field items; proof + arrows-into + premises-for for Results to redo.
export function redoLimits(step: number, items: readonly SessionItemRecord[]): StepLimits;
export interface JudgeInput {
  purpose: 'check'|'freeze'|'gate-proved'|'gate-other'|'stage'|'final';
  base: ProjectModel; current: ProjectModel; stepStart?: ProjectModel; limits?: StepLimits; freeze?: FrozenSnapshot;
  inferences: readonly SessionInference[]; ledger: TeleleanLedger; items: ReadonlyMap<string, SessionItemRecord>; subject: string;
}
export interface InferenceJudgement {
  target: string; verdict: 'established'|'proved'|'not-proved';
  notEstablishedBecause?: Array<'rests-on-pending'|'conditional'|'hidden-assumption'|'unsure'>;
  proofPresent: boolean; passes: boolean; permitted: InferencePermitted; direct?: DirectUses; footprint: string[];
  restsOn: string[]; throughResults: string[]; notNeeded: string[]; provedFromNothing: boolean;
  replacesYourProof: boolean; provesChangedStatement: boolean; findings: GateFinding[];
}
export interface StateJudgement { global: GateFinding[]; inferences: ReadonlyMap<string, InferenceJudgement>; stepFindings: GateFinding[]; passed: boolean }
export function judgeState(i: JudgeInput): StateJudgement;
export function proposeArrowProblems(state: ProjectModel, limits: StepLimits, ledger: TeleleanLedger, items: ReadonlyMap<string, SessionItemRecord>, source: string, target: string): string[];
```
**Global rules** (helpers extracted from gate/rules.ts):
- **G0 and G1:** as today, with B as the baseline. Claude's earlier content never counts as "yours".
- **new-axiom (against B):** an axiom of S is acceptable only if it is one of:
  - (i) a B axiom with the same name and normalised type;
  - (ii) a new sort or predicate that passes the shape rule;
  - (iii) a presupposition T.exists of a sort;
  - (iv) the .holds of an AXIOM card whose statement is new in the session (it states exactly the statement), or of a ledger 'premise' card;
  - (v) a PROPOSITION's .holds axiom that is ledger-written or unchanged from B.
  Anything else is a finding with token belief, pending or unclassified (S6).
- **preset** (step purposes; replaces existing-changed): every declaration of P keeps its text, kind, normalised type and value, and its valueConsts and typeConsts sets, unless an opening covers it. Tokens: changed, meaning, removed, target-statement.
- **kind (B.4):**
  - `type:` never changes, whether compared P→S or B→S;
  - a .holds goes from axiom to theorem only under proof(T), with the identical type, and never from theorem to axiom;
  - with gate-other, T.holds stays byte-identical to P, so removal is caught too (status-mismatch extended).
- **arrow (B.3, AR-5):** the `premises:` and `follows_from:` differences P→S are exactly this step's ledger entries.
  - Each entry targets an arrows-into opening.
  - It never points into an AXIOM or into a target whose question is its mark.
  - Its source is an axiom or proposition of the subject that has a .holds, and the arrow was not declined before (DO-0).
  - The drawn + solid arrows of S are acyclic (arrowCycleThrough). A cycle already in B is never counted as Claude's attempt (AP-13).
- **markup (G5/CF-3):** markupFindings against P, with the ledger replacing adoptedPremises, adoptedMarkRemoved and teleleanBlocks. New blocks are allowed only for ledger premises. At 'final' it compares against B.
- **footprint:** every new or changed declaration is judged against the permitted set of the inference of the step that created it (ledger 'created'). Proofs must fit exactly; other declarations may also use the presuppositions (as allowedForOthers does today).
- **sorry, examples, vocabulary-shape** (now also for changed items) and **proof-before-freeze** (R = P): as today.
- **repeat:** an item whose key equals one of its rejectedKeys (DO-1). A Shaky replacement set identical to the declined set, comparing kinds, sentences, Lean statements and arrows with whitespace collapsed (DO-3), unless Claude reports that it found no alternative.

**Per inference** (every purpose, every inference, sources first):
- footprint(T.holds) ⊆ permitted(T) (`footprint`);
- B.2 `undeclared-premise` with allowed = sources(Q ∪ E), plus unseen and source-only;
- not-proved at gate-proved, for the active step;
- statement-changed and G4 for the active step only (other inferences' statements are under the preset).

**What stepFindings contains:** global findings plus the active inference's findings. Other inferences' outcomes feed RV-11 updates and never fail a step.

**Gate contract changes:** GateFindingCode (gate/types.ts:18) gains 'preset', 'arrow', 'kind' and 'repeat'; GateFinding gets an optional `inference`; describe.ts gets board sentences. evaluateRules stays as the single-inference adapter, so the M2 and 1e tests keep guarding regressions.

