- "‹decl› changed, but no review item covers it."
- "‹decl› belongs to ‹item›, which is not accepted."
- "‹item› needs its own Accept (belief / changes what is proved)."
- "‹item› changed after you accepted it."
- "telelean could not see what the final statements rely on."

## D10. Persistence (ES-6)
Stored outside ws/ (run dir or VS Code storage), so it is never in Claude's working copy:
- base-facts.json and step-<n>-facts.json;
- the ledger;
- the SessionItemRecords (status, accepted key and how, rejectedKeys, decline option, forced reveal);
- the SessionInferences (question, order, startHolds).

On reload, ownership, keys, classes, the graph and the hidden set are recomputed from the shadow head and its facts. An accepted item whose key differs returns to in-review ("updated"). Persisted statuses are never trusted on their own.

